        a                       ecrm:E12_Production ;
        rdfs:comment            "The upholstery is of the highest quality and attributed to the upholsterer Francis Lapiere, the design is probably by William III's architect and interior designer, Daniel Marot (1661-1752)\n\nAttribution note: The bed relates to designs published by Daniel Marot in the Nouveaus Livres d'Apartements, Amsterdam, 1702 and reissued in 1712. It is likely that the bed was made up from original drawings by Daniel Marot as it is believed that the creation of this bed precedes the publication of Daniel Marot's designs for State Beds.\nReason For Production: Commission" ;
        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/05606757-beff-3e1a-b594-cc083530c640> ;
